    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0402" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.24/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-14T11:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                                1925—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:54
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Your February 6, 5 p.m. President Baraona showed me signed letter. It
                    authorizes Luis Bográn: (1) to state that the Government of Honduras undertakes
                    to organize constabulary and to employ American instructors and (2) to contract
                    for the purchase of arms. I am forwarding a copy of this letter by pouch.<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d269-f1"/></p>
                <p>Several legal experts, including government officials, whom I consulted, agree
                    that President Baraona’s authorization to Luis Bográn to contract is sufficient
                    to bind Government of Honduras respecting the <pb facs="0403" n="321"
                        xml:id="pg321"/> consular revenues without the approval of the Honduran
                    Congress. This opinion has been confirmed by President Baraona.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d269-f1" n="12" xml:id="d269-f1-content">
                <p>Letter to Bográn not printed; it is dated February 13.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
